    },
    {
      "id": "EA6abwnB9JZ2R_oraytrT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 212,
      "y": 1587.734375,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0u",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1973187784,
      "version": 8,
      "versionNonce": 2146950840,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794404584290,
      "created": 1794404574006,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "By using a time bucket (Unix timestamp rounded down to the nearest hour) as\nour partition key, we can efficiently query for upcoming jobs. We only need to\nquery the current hour's bucket and possibly the next hour's bucket. The time\nbucket can be easily calculated:\n\ntime_bucket = (execution_time // 3600) * 3600  # Round down to nearest hour",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "By using a time bucket (Unix timestamp rounded down to the nearest hour) as our partition key, we can efficiently query for upcoming jobs. We only need to query the current hour's bucket and possibly the next hour's bucket. The time bucket can be easily calculated:\n\ntime_bucket = (execution_time // 3600) * 3600  # Round down to nearest hour",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ElFUR4vZkwVROCd4oPHpO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 132,
      "y": 1985.6171875,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 271453128,
      "version": 13,
      "versionNonce": 1854080184,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794445727609,
      "created": 1794445709629,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "==Flow==\nA user creates a new job which is written to the database.\nA cron job runs every 5 minutes to query the database for jobs that are due for\nexecution in the next ~5 minutes.\nThe cron job sends these jobs to SQS with appropriate delay values (SQS\nsupports delays up to 15 minutes, so our 5-minute window fits comfortably).\nWorkers continuously poll SQS and process messages as they become visible.\nIf a new job is created with a scheduled time < 5 minutes from the current time,\nit's sent directly to SQS with the appropriate delay.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "==Flow==\nA user creates a new job which is written to the database.\nA cron job runs every 5 minutes to query the database for jobs that are due for execution in the next ~5 minutes.\nThe cron job sends these jobs to SQS with appropriate delay values (SQS supports delays up to 15 minutes, so our 5-minute window fits comfortably).\nWorkers continuously poll SQS and process messages as they become visible.\nIf a new job is created with a scheduled time < 5 minutes from the current time, it's sent directly to SQS with the appropriate delay.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
